# Fleet votes with callbacks days or weeks later. House style: content/STYLE.md.
# Both sides of every vote are reasonable people being reasonable.

# --- Fleet portrait -----------------------------------------------------------
card dec_photo
type decision
cat mission
days 6 24
weight 8
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean warm fly decline
text Public affairs wants a fleet portrait: seven ships in one frame, with Earth behind them. It costs propellant to fly the formation. The request uses the word "iconic" four times.
option fly | Fly the formation | Seven ships close to formation distance for eleven minutes. {A} takes the shot from a camera on {A}'s ship. Nobody breathes until the ships are apart again.
  set photo_taken
  res fuel -2
  morale A 4
option decline | Politely decline | The fleet sends a polite no and a very good photo of a single ship. Public affairs replies with one word: "Noted."
  set photo_declined

card photo_back
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 18 40
roles A
when flag photo_taken
when cond A ok
text The fleet portrait made the front page of every news site on Earth, 20 minutes ago. {A} zooms in and finds their own ship: a small bright dot, third from the left.
do morale A 5

# --- Water recovery -------------------------------------------------------
card dec_water
type decision
cat repair
days 8 26
weight 9
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean brave degrade strip
when cond A ok
text Water recovery on {A}'s ship is down to 93 percent from 98. {A} wants to strip the processor now. {B} wants to run it degraded and fix it when things are calmer. Out here, things don't get calmer.
option strip | Strip it now | The processor spends nine hours in pieces on the deck. {A} finds a clogged filter and a check valve installed backwards at the factory. Recovery is back to 98 percent by dinner.
  set water_fixed
  res spares -1
  trait A curious 3
option degrade | Run it degraded | The fleet goes on water rationing. Nobody complains out loud. {A} logs the recovery rate every hour, which is its own kind of complaint.
  set water_rationed
  who water_who A
  morale A -3

card water_fail
type event
cat repair
due
once
days 18 40
roles A B
when flag water_rationed
when is A water_who
when apart B A
when cond B ok
text The degraded water processor on {A}'s ship quits at 04:00. {A} has the rebuild plan taped inside the panel door, already written. {B} crosses over with the spare valve, and the two of them have water flowing by breakfast.
do move B A
do bond A B 8
do res spares -1
do clr water_rationed

# --- Clocks -----------------------------------------------------------------
card dec_clock
type decision
cat mission
days 4 30
weight 6
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious shift keep
text Mission Control proposes moving the fleet's clocks two hours forward, to line up with the ground team's shifts. {A} is for it. {B} has seen this study before.
option shift | Change the clocks | The fleet shifts its clocks. Everyone is tired for three days and then fine, exactly as the study predicted and nobody believed.
  set clock_shifted
option keep | Keep fleet time | The fleet keeps its clocks. The ground team adjusts instead, and sends a photo of the night shift's pizza as evidence.
  set clock_kept

# --- Course correction -------------------------------------------------------
card dec_trim
type decision
cat mission
days 12 28
weight 9
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean brave now wait
text Navigation shows the fleet drifting toward the edge of the arrival corridor. {A} wants a small correction burn now. {B} wants to wait for the scheduled burn, which costs more but leaves time to check the solution three times.
option now | Burn now | A short, clean burn. {A} watches the residuals come in under a tenth of a meter per second and allows a single fist pump.
  set trim_early
  res fuel -1
option wait | Wait and check | The solution gets checked three times, then a fourth. The scheduled burn goes off on time and on target, and {B} lets the computer fly it.
  set trim_late
  res fuel -3

card trim_callback
type event
cat mission
due
once
days 29 40
roles A
when fired dec_trim
when cond A ok
when trait A curious >= -10
text The final navigation fix comes in: the fleet sits within a few kilometers of the center of the arrival corridor. {A} reads the number twice, then pins it to the wall beside Earth's last decent photo.
do morale A 3

# --- Arrival: dust storm over the landing region -------------------------------
card dust_report
type event
cat arrival
days 29 36
weight 22
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} pulls the morning weather from the Mars orbiters: a regional dust storm, building over the landing zone. On the map it's a brown thumbprint. {A} measures it against the zone with a ruler, and then measures it again.
do set dust_seen

card dec_arrival
type decision
cat arrival
days 33 38
weight 10
once
duration 2
roles A B
when flag dust_seen
lean brave hold wait
text The dust storm over the landing zone is still growing. {A} wants to hold the arrival plan and trust the margins. {B} wants to burn for a longer capture orbit and wait it out, at a real cost in propellant.
option hold | Hold the plan | The arrival plan stands. {A} runs the entry numbers for the worst-case dust load and posts them where everyone can see.
  set arrive_hold
option wait | Long orbit, wait | The fleet commits to the long orbit. {B} recomputes every margin. They are thinner than anyone would like, and they are enough.
  set arrive_wait
  res fuel -4
